<title>VENEZUELA: President of Venezuela's Sidor resigns - paper.</title>
<headline>President of Venezuela's Sidor resigns - paper.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The President of Venezuelan state- owned steel company Sidor that is due to be privatized early next year has resigned, leading daily El Universal reported.</p>
<p>Teolindo Yanez, who ran Sidor from April 1995, tendered his resignation Monday night and will be replaced by Sidor vice- president Alfredo Rivas Lairet, El Universal reported.</p>
<p>Sidor is due to be privatized in the first of 1997, along with four aluminum companies in the Corporacion Venezolana de Guayana's (CVG) industrial complex. No reason was given for Yanez's resignation.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
